{
  "requirement": "Every domain supplies its validation cache through `Domain::cache`. Repeated\ncalls on the domain and its clones provide access to the same cached outlines\nand agent configuration.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.cache`.\n\n**Obligations from the requirement text**\n1. A domain supplies its cache through `Domain::cache`.\n2. Calls on the domain and on its clones reach the same cached outlines.\n3. Calls on the domain and on its clones reach the same agent configuration.\n\n**Outlines**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` builds an `Application` domain around a cache, then clones it as `peer`.\n- It caches `other.rs` through `peer.cache()`. It then deletes both files from disk.\n- `domain.cache()` still returns the cached `other.rs` text.\n- `peer.cache()` also serves the cached first snapshot of `lib.rs`, after the file was rewritten and then deleted. `std::ptr::eq` on the outlines confirms it is the same snapshot.\n- A separate `Application::default().cache()` sees the new file contents. This shows the sharing comes from clones and not from a global cache.\n- Together these assertions show that the domain and its clone share one outline cache through `cache()`. They would fail if `cache()` returned a fresh or per-clone cache.\n\n**Agent configuration**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]` clones a `TestDomain` whose cache holds an agent.\n- It asserts `Arc::ptr_eq` on `domain.cache().agent` and `peer.cache().agent`. It also asserts that the peer's agent config equals the original config.\n- This directly checks that the clone provides the same agent configuration.\n\n**Every domain**\n- `ValidationCache` derives `Clone` over `Arc` fields, so a clone shares the same cache state.\n- The tests use `Domain` implementations whose `cache()` returns a stored cache field: `Application` in `contracts.rs` and `TestDomain` in `configured.rs`.\n- The trait method has no conditional of its own, so no further per-implementation tests are needed.\n\nI found no gap. Both tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement.",
